# Guard, not the real configuration.
#
# The portal is deployed with the Vercel project's Root Directory set to
# `admin-web`, and in that setup Vercel reads admin-web/.vercelignore and never
# looks at this file. This one only takes effect if somebody deploys from the
# repository root by mistake -- `vercel` run from here, or the Root Directory
# left unset -- which would otherwise publish the SQL migrations, the Flutter
# source and the planning documents as static files on a public URL.
#
# Ignore everything, then allow back only the directory that is meant to ship.
*
!admin-web
!admin-web/**
admin-web/tests
